{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>El</b> — The word <b>el</b> is <b>tapkek</b> [an adverb/particle of negation]; it serves on account of another. Likewise is <b>zamamo el tapkek al yerommu sela</b> [their scheme—let it not rise, selah] — it and what resembles it. Or <b>tapkek</b> may be joined to <b>rosh</b> [<b>al taqshir rosh</b>, 'do not place a head'], and <b>yerommu</b> comes in place of <b>yerum</b>. And Rabbi Moses said: <b>roshim</b> ['heads'] means what will befall my oppressors: <b>'amal sifteyhem yekhasem</b> [the trouble of their lips will cover them]. And the meaning is that they boast, for <b>ya'akhezuni bamoqshim</b> [they seize me with snares]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 140, :notes {0 "The text is elliptical and compressed throughout; Ibn Ezra is debating whether 'el' in this verse is the negative particle 'al' (tapkek), and whether 'roshim' means 'heads' in some technical sense or refers to what befalls the enemies. 'Rabbi Moses' likely refers to Moses Ibn Ezra or Moses ha-Kohen; resolving by inference."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:26.485914660Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}